{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_gameplay_redesign", "label": "Gameplay & scripting redesign", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Net result: ~7 systems + 3 storages + 3 types collapse into 2 systems + 1 component + thin handles."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_shadow_ecs_problem", "label": "Shadow ECS (4 copies of one datum)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ScriptComponentStorage was a second ECS over Nexus: duplicate types, a duplicate vector type (Vector2D vs Vec2), and a diff/request/feedback machine whose only job was copying one into the other, with per-entity per-frame allocations in the hot path."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_unity_interop_misreading", "label": "Unity C++\u2194C# split is a proxy, not a copy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unity's C# Transform is a thin handle whose accessors cross interop and read/write the C++ memory directly \u2014 one source of truth, a window on it. That split exists because a hard technical frontier (managed/GC vs native) forces it; in TypeScript there is no such frontier, so the cost of separation was paid without the constraint that justifies it."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_thin_facade_handle", "label": "Thin fa\u00e7ade handle", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A handle holds no data, only (world, entity), so `this.transform.position.x += 10` mutates the single source of truth \u2014 encapsulation kept, sync deleted. Fa\u00e7ades are reserved for ENGINE components (authority/encapsulation); user data components like Health are accessed directly."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_transform2dcomponent", "label": "Transform2DComponent fa\u00e7ade", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_rigidbody2dcomponent", "label": "RigidBody2DComponent fa\u00e7ade", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_scriptcomponentregistry", "label": "ScriptComponentRegistry (lazy resolve + event-invalidated cache)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only a found instance is cached, never absence, so a later addComponent is seen on next access without listening to onAdd; onRemove invalidates. Re-resolving every access would already be negligible at target scale \u2014 the cache is an optimisation, not a requirement."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_setcomponent_mutate_in_place", "label": "Contract: mutate in place, never replace", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "world.setComponent replaces the instance without emitting onRemove, the one operation that would silently stale the handle cache; the alternative is hardening Nexus to emit onRemove+onAdd on replacement."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_physicsbodyref", "label": "PhysicsBodyRef component", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turning the inertia body handle into a normal Nexus component lets queries join it and lets onRemove destroy the body \u2014 deleting the hand-managed SparseSet and the manual plugin hook. Runtime-only, never serialized."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_physicspushsystem", "label": "PhysicsPushSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Creates missing bodies (via world.commands since it iterates) and pushes velocity plus, for kinematic/static, position/rotation into the solver."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_physicspullsystem", "label": "PhysicsPullSystem", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes back only for dynamic bodies; reading kinematic back would recreate a second authority over the same datum."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_authority_by_body_type", "label": "Authority declared by body type", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'What if I move both at once' disappears: per entity exactly one authority owns position, decided at write time by reading RigidBody2D.type. Dynamic is moved by velocity/force and setPosition is an explicit teleport, never a silent clobber."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_vec2_unification", "label": "Vec2 everywhere (Vector2D deleted)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vector2D existed only to serve the shadow layer and was copied field by field into Vec2; removing the shadow layer removed the need for it."}, {"id": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_dynamic_teleport_risk", "label": "Dynamic teleport before body creation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On the first frame PhysicsBodyRef may not exist yet, so setPosition must fall back to writing Transform2D (used as the initial translation at body creation) instead of calling a non-existent body."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_scriptcomponentregistry", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_lifecycle_events", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_physicspushsystem", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_typed_query", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_physicspushsystem", "target": "docs_core_nexus_ecs_command_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_gameplay_redesign", "target": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_redesign_shadow_ecs_problem", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/gameplay/gameplay-redesign.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_gameplay_gameplay_re